findings.claim:
Two accepted routes give the Cohen structure theorem different owners, and route 7's reason misstates R03.1. CS-24 (and BHATT-MATHEW-23/080) send it to R03.1 as a source. BHATT-18 sends the same mixed-characteristic statement to the new roadmap DirectSummandsAndBigCohenMacaulay, whose design is pending. Route 7's reason says R03.1 builds 'presentations of complete local rings as quotients of power series rings'. R03.1, narrowed by the accepted RS-08, keeps only:
- coefficient categories of complete local O-algebras with a fixed identification of the residue field;
- their presentation 'as the inverse limit of its Artinian quotients';
- 'continuous maps from power-series rings'.
It has neither the existence of coefficient (Cohen) rings for an arbitrary complete Noetherian local ring nor the classification of complete regular local rings as W(k)⟦x⟧/(p − f), and that is what /004 states. Meanwhile the PerfectoidSpaces P0–P7 packet records the theorem as a gap with no owner, and its new P7 nodes for Česnavičius's Lemmas 5.1–5.2 (the towers of CS-24/037) depend on it. Severity set to medium by the coordinator: a single-item duplicate, treated as medium in the earlier red teams.

Grothendieck's parafactoriality theorem, SGA 2 XI 3.13(ii) with its factoriality corollary 3.14, has three accepted owners:
- CS-24 plans it in the new roadmap (/133, layer 7);
- CESNAVICIUS-19 sends it to SF.4 (local-pic-lefschetz);
- two further accepted extractions send it as a source to DeformationAndDerivedPatchingAlgebra R03.1/R03.3.
The confirmed RT-PAPER-CESNAVICIUS-19/1 settles only the first two, so its fix does not reach the R03 routes, and the R03 blueprint would plan the theorem again. Its proof needs SGA 2's formal Lefschetz machinery, which none of R03's stages plans. Severity set to medium by the coordinator: a single-item duplicate, treated as medium in the earlier red teams.

The briefs import from roadmap ids that will never exist, and the design jobs are not ordered. make_queue merges every Part II with the same parent into one job whose roadmap id is '<parent>PartII'. So SchemeAndStackFoundationsFlatCohomologyPartII, PerfectoidQuotientsIntegralPerfectoidPartII, EtaleDualityAbsolutePurityPartII and PrismaticCohomologyPartIIPrismaticDieudonneTheory never become roadmaps. Yet:
- routes 1 and 2 import 'PrismaticCohomologyPartIIPrismaticDieudonneTheory' by that id;
- routes 1, 3 and 4 import 'this extraction's' sibling Part IIs only by description;
- no brief names the other proposals each Part II is merged with: Bhatt–Scholze route 3 for PerfectoidQuotients; CESNAVICIUS-21, BHATT-ETAL-23, HACON-WITASZEK-23, BAKKER-TSIMERMAN-16 and GUO-REINECKE-24 for SchemeAndStackFoundations; the stacks and ind-constructible proposals for EtaleDualityAndPerverseSheaves.
The merged Scheme job is told to 'plan the first here and record a restructure proposal for the rest', so the flat-cohomology Part II may be deferred while DESIGN-PurityForFlatCohomology, which has no 'after', designs against it. RT-PAPER-CESNAVICIUS-21/1 (confirmed) found the same defect in that paper's routes.

